   454	# All four are required. The fourth is not redundant: it is the ONLY watcher
   455	# of the SBOM/SECURITY/VERSIONING stamps, which are outside the VERSION_SITES
   456	# of verify-counts. Without it an external no-op would block the in-loop
   457	# self-heal from ever running over a stale stamp. Freezing the DATE is safe
   458	# because the freshness gate decides on the stamp VERSION, not its date.
