   176	    # PER-DOCUMENT expectation set (pair-rail R3, P2). Aggregate liveness
   177	    # is a FLOOR: a metric matching 5 of 6 watched docs looks alive while
   178	    # the 6th drifts — exactly how docs/GUIA-COMPLETO.md sat stale at 44
   179	    # hooks AFTER the metric-level rule was "fixed". These pairs are the
   180	    # sites that actually carry each claim today; dropping one is a
   181	    # silent coverage loss, so it must fail here and be re-ratified
   182	    # deliberately (add/remove a pair) rather than vanish.
   183	    # EXHAUSTIVE manifest, with EXACT counts (pair-rail R5). Two earlier
   184	    # shapes of this guard were still vacuous:
   185	    #   - covering 3 metrics of the 54 live pairs left every unlisted
   186	    #     claim (skills@INSTALL.md, hook_py@CLAUDE.md, …) able to drift
   187	    #     while aggregate rule_matches stayed nonzero from other docs;
   188	    #   - asserting PRESENCE (>=1) let a doc carrying TWO independent
   189	    #     claims for one metric (registered@docs/ARCHITECTURE.md: table +
   190	    #     prose) lose one silently.
   191	    # So: every pair, with its exact count. Editing a watched doc is
   192	    # SUPPOSED to fail here — that forces the manifest to be re-ratified
   193	    # deliberately instead of coverage evaporating unnoticed. Regenerate
   194	    # with: verify-counts.sh --json --no-tests | jq .rule_matches_by_doc
   195	    # RE-RATIFIED at the PLAN-166 W0 reconciliation: the W0 doc pass added
   196	    # count claims to README.pt-BR.md, docs/CTO-GUIDE.md, docs/README.md,
   197	    # docs/WHAT-WE-ARE.md, docs/FAQ.md and npm/README.md, growing the census
   198	    # from 54 to 109 pairs. Regenerated from the gate itself (never typed from
   199	    # memory); the ratification asserted ZERO lost and ZERO shrunk pairs
   200	    # first, so coverage only widened.
