     1	#!/usr/bin/env python3
     2	"""debate-converge.py — Jaccard convergence detector for debate rounds.
     3	
     4	PLAN-011 Phase 5. Detects when a debate has converged by computing the
     5	Jaccard similarity of the risk sets between round N and round N-1
     6	across all agent critique files.
     7	
     8	## Usage
     9	
    10	    debate-converge.py --plan PLAN-NNN --round N [--plans-root <path>]
    11	
    12	    N must be >= 2. Round N-1 must exist on disk.
    13	
    14	## Algorithm
    15	
    16	1. For round N and round N-1, read every `<archetype>.md` file under
    17	   `.claude/plans/PLAN-NNN/debate/round-<N>/` (excluding `proposal.md`,
    18	   `consensus.md`, `synthesis.md`, `red-team.md` — those are CEO/meta
    19	   artifacts, not agent critiques).
    20	2. In each file, locate the `## Risks` heading and extract bullet items
    21	   (lines starting with `- `). Continue through subsequent bullets
    22	   until a new heading (`## `) or EOF.
    23	3. Normalize each risk bullet: lowercase, strip punctuation, collapse
    24	   whitespace, dedupe within a file.
    25	4. Union all risk bullets per round into a set.
    26	5. Compute Jaccard = |A ∩ B| / |A ∪ B| (0 if both sets are empty).
    27	6. Output JSON: `{"jaccard": float, "converged": bool, "red_team_needed": bool}`.
    28	
    29	`converged` is True iff jaccard >= threshold (default 0.7).
    30	`red_team_needed` is True iff `converged AND round <= 2`. This is the
    31	M1 anti-groupthink gate from PLAN-011 consensus round 1.
    32	
    33	## Why 0.7
    34	
    35	See ADR-032 §Decision drivers. 0.7 means ~70% of the risk vocabulary
    36	overlaps between rounds — high enough to distinguish "same topics
    37	reordered" from "genuine agreement". Lower thresholds (0.5) would
    38	declare convergence on largely disjoint sets; higher (0.9) would
    39	require near-exact text, which rarely survives Round→Round agent
    40	paraphrase.
    41	
    42	## Exit codes
    43	
    44	    0 — convergence computed successfully (JSON printed to stdout)
    45	    1 — bad args / round < 2 / round N-1 missing
    46	    2 — no agent critique files found in either round (zero coverage)
    47	    3 — max_rounds_reached (terminal; orchestrator also exits 3)
    48	"""
