   153	# Whitelist validation: letters, digits, space, underscore, dash, plus —
   154	# PLAN-169 W2.3 [codex r12-P2] — slash and ampersand, because the REAL
   155	# roster contains "UI/UX Lead" and "Accessibility & i18n Engineer" and the
   156	# old charset rejected both. First char must be a letter; max 61 chars.
   157	# Dot stays OUT of the charset, so path traversal via the name remains
   158	# impossible by construction; downstream the name is only (a) compared
   159	# fixed-string/equality-wise and (b) used as a KEY into the fixed
   160	# name->slug table — never interpolated into a path or a regex.
   161	# Whole-string bash =~, NOT a grep pipe: grep matches PER LINE, so a name
   162	# carrying an embedded newline ("a\nb") was ACCEPTED — each line matched
