     1	# SPEC v1 — debate.schema
     2	
     3	> **Normative source:** `.claude/plans/DEBATE-SCHEMA.md`
     4	> **Spec version:** 1.0.0-rc.1
     5	
     6	## Summary (normative)
     7	
     8	Multi-round debate artifacts on disk at
     9	`.claude/plans/PLAN-<NNN>/debate/round-N/`:
    10	
    11	- `proposal.md` (round 1 only)
    12	- `<archetype-slug>.md` (one per participating archetype)
    13	- `consensus.md` per round
    14	- `synthesis.md` for a round-3 terminal synthesis
    15	
    16	Each critique file has frontmatter (`round`, `archetype`, `skill`,
    17	`agent_persona`, `generated_at`) + 7 required body sections (`Verdict`,
    18	`Summary`, `Risks`, `Must-fix`, `Nice-to-have`, `Unseen`, `What I would
    19	NOT change`).
    20	
    21	Consensus files have frontmatter (`plan`, `round`, `rounds_synthesized`,
    22	`agents_considered`, `decisions_revised_in_plan`, `synthesized_at`,
    23	`synthesized_by`) + body sections enumerating consensus findings,
    24	single-agent insights kept, insights deferred, plan adjustments, and
    25	a round verdict (`PROCEED` | `RUN-ANOTHER-ROUND` | `ESCALATE-TO-OWNER`).
    26	
    27	For the full contract including the 3-round maximum and the
    28	same-LLM-forced-perspective rationale, read
    29	`.claude/plans/DEBATE-SCHEMA.md`.
    30	
    31	## Version history
    32	
    33	| SPEC version | Source commit | Notes |
    34	|---|---|---|
    35	| 1.0.0-rc.1 | Sprint 4 opening | Initial published contract; default 3 archetypes per round, with exceptional 6-archetype round 1 permitted for maximally cross-cutting plans (see PLAN-004/debate/round-1/consensus.md) |
